    <header class="about-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Hello, I'm Jacob</p><h1>Hi, I'm Jacob.</h1><p class="lead">Books, personal reflections, gaming, and the interests that keep life interesting. Welcome to my corner of the internet.</p></header>
    <div class="about-story creator-about-story"><h2>A few interests. One home base.</h2><p>J Sol is where I share what I’m reading, things I’m thinking through, and a little gaming and downtime. Books, reflections and play are the main threads, with room for small discoveries along the way.</p><p>Start with <a href="/#book-vote">Pick My Next Book</a>, explore a few <a href="/#recent-videos">published videos</a>, or find my writing and reading profiles below. You don’t have to choose just one interest.</p></div>
    <PublicProfiles />
    <div class="about-story">
      <section aria-labelledby="engineering-title"><p class="eyebrow">Alongside the creator work</p><h2 id="engineering-title">Engineering &amp; consulting</h2><p>I have more than seven years of professional technology experience across site reliability engineering, monitoring and observability, cloud infrastructure, DevOps and automation. I’m also a small-business owner.</p><h3>Good systems should give something back.</h3><p>Time. Attention. A little less repetitive work. That is the idea behind my practical systems notes and professional work.</p><p>The existing <a href="/guides">AI, technology and automation guides</a>, <a href="/resources">project toolkit</a> and <a href="/consulting">Monitoring &amp; Alert Health Check</a> remain available if that is what brought you here.</p></section>
      <h2>Why stockswatch.cc?</h2><p>This domain started as an investment-research experiment called StocksWatch. The focus has changed. J Sol is now its home, and the old market-data desk and paid-product preview are retired.</p><p>Reusing a domain is one small way to keep the project simple. There is no investment service or financial advice offered here.</p><h2>The rule for growing</h2><p>Start small. Build something useful. Learn what people want. Add more only when there is evidence to justify the work.</p><p>This is an independent personal project. It does not speak for an employer or disclose private workplace or customer information.</p>
    </div>
